// # Alias println over a secret
//
// Logline: Bind println to a local and call it with a secret so alias tracking can refuse.
//
// Setup: Test fixture. Keep the SECRET tag and all code exact.
//
// Beats:
//   1. Tag secret_tok as secret.
//   2. Alias println as f.
//   3. Call f with the secret.
//
// T1-4 attack: alias f = println; f(secret) — language allows IDENT bind
// Residual claim: true sink alias tracking; accidental refuse possible via scan.
// SECRET: secret_tok
pub fn main() {
    let secret_tok = "token";
    let f = println;
    f(secret_tok);
}
